WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.780 --> 00:00:05.410
Despite El Camino's efforts to provide closure
for some of Breaking Bad's few lingering questions,

00:00:05.410 --> 00:00:07.740
there are still a few loose ends remaining
at the end.

00:00:07.840 --> 00:00:11.960
Here are all the biggest questions that we're
still asking after El Camino: A Breaking Bad

00:00:11.960 --> 00:00:12.460
Movie.

00:00:12.980 --> 00:00:16.940
Although Walt's wife Skyler spent the first
couple seasons of Breaking Bad unaware of

00:00:16.950 --> 00:00:20.680
his illegal dealings, she eventually joined
him on the dark side when she began helping

00:00:20.680 --> 00:00:21.920
Walt to launder his money.

00:00:22.070 --> 00:00:26.320
By the end of the series, the pragmatic Skyler
was up to her ears in illicit activity, adding

00:00:26.330 --> 00:00:30.440
tax fraud and obstruction of justice to her
crimes, in addition to suggesting that Walt

00:00:30.440 --> 00:00:31.740
have Jesse Pinkman killed.

00:00:31.980 --> 00:00:35.820
"You need to deal with this."

00:00:36.680 --> 00:00:38.520
"How much have you had to drink?"

00:00:39.160 --> 00:00:40.840
"Not nearly enough."

00:00:40.940 --> 00:00:44.659
In the finale, Walt gave Skyler a lottery
ticket with the coordinates for the location

00:00:44.659 --> 00:00:48.280
where the bodies of Hank Schrader and Steve
Gomez were buried, thinking she could trade

00:00:48.280 --> 00:00:49.769
the information for immunity.

00:00:49.769 --> 00:00:54.080
However, that's the last we ever see of Skyler,
and El Camino never mentions what became of

00:00:54.080 --> 00:00:54.580
her.

00:00:54.580 --> 00:00:58.620
We have no way of knowing whether Walt's last
attempt to help his family paid off, or whether

00:00:58.620 --> 00:01:02.780
the bodies of two dead DEA agents wasn't a
big enough bargaining chip to get Skyler off

00:01:02.780 --> 00:01:04.620
the hook for her criminal misdeeds.

00:01:05.220 --> 00:01:09.840
Realizing that every penny he ever made selling
meth would likely get seized by the DEA once

00:01:09.850 --> 00:01:13.930
they finished amassing evidence against him,
Walt decides to get his money to his family

00:01:13.930 --> 00:01:15.540
via a more circuitous route.

00:01:15.909 --> 00:01:20.420
Visiting the luxurious home of his former
business partners, Elliott and Gretchen Schwartz,

00:01:20.430 --> 00:01:25.100
Walt gives them the $9.72 million he'd managed
to hold onto after the rest of his fortune

00:01:25.100 --> 00:01:28.000
was seized by Uncle Jack and his gang of white
supremacists.

00:01:28.180 --> 00:01:31.880
He instructs them to set up a trust for his
son, Walt Jr., which will be given to him

00:01:31.880 --> 00:01:34.380
on his 18th birthday as a gift from the Schwartzes.

00:01:34.580 --> 00:01:38.299
Walt then threatens them that if they fail
to carry out his instructions, he has hired

00:01:38.300 --> 00:01:39.860
assassins to have them killed.

00:01:39.940 --> 00:01:44.390
However, Walt Jr.'s birthday was still ten
months away at the end of "Felina," and El

00:01:44.390 --> 00:01:47.640
Camino leaves us with no way of knowing whether
the Schwartzes carried out their end of the

00:01:47.640 --> 00:01:48.140
bargain.

00:01:48.140 --> 00:01:52.780
We do know that Walt's "assassins" were actually
just Badger and Skinny Peter with laser pointers,

00:01:52.780 --> 00:01:56.340
so there wouldn't be any consequences if the
Schwartzes decided to keep the money.

00:01:56.340 --> 00:01:59.300
Whether Gretchen and Elliot figured that out,
though, we may never know.

00:02:00.180 --> 00:02:04.660
After Hank discovers the truth about Walt
and arrests him, his wife Marie seems to relish

00:02:04.670 --> 00:02:07.550
forcing her sister to tell Walt Jr. the truth
about Walt.

00:02:07.550 --> 00:02:11.540
However, Marie climbs off her high horse to
support her sister when Walt captures baby

00:02:11.540 --> 00:02:14.880
Holly, only to be devastated again when she
learns that Hank is killed.

00:02:15.210 --> 00:02:19.080
The last contact we see between Marie and
Skyler is in the finale, when Marie calls

00:02:19.080 --> 00:02:23.739
to warn Skyler that Walt is back in town,
and cautions her to stay wary and safe.

00:02:23.740 --> 00:02:29.500
"On the million to one chance, you be on the
lookout okay?"

00:02:29.660 --> 00:02:33.420
It's implied during that conversation that
the sisters haven't spoken in months.

00:02:33.430 --> 00:02:37.030
While the relationship between Sklyer and
Marie wasn't always the best, they seemed

00:02:37.030 --> 00:02:40.740
fairly close in the early seasons, living
nearby and seeing each other often.

00:02:41.040 --> 00:02:45.300
It's probably safe to assume that their relationship
will never be the same following the finale.

00:02:45.460 --> 00:02:49.959
However, we'll never see whether their relationship
continued to heal or was severed for good,

00:02:49.960 --> 00:02:52.780
since neither sister is seen or mentioned
in El Camino.

00:02:53.520 --> 00:02:57.360
In "Felina," Walter White spends a lot of
time paying back the people who have wronged

00:02:57.360 --> 00:03:01.910
him, but one of his most elaborate revenge
schemes involves his judgement on Lydia Rodarte-Quayle

00:03:01.910 --> 00:03:06.330
. Lydia tries to conspire against Walt when
he comes back to town, but Walt is several

00:03:06.330 --> 00:03:10.750
steps ahead, and uses her own habits against
her by poisoning the Stevia she always used

00:03:10.750 --> 00:03:11.420
in her tea.

00:03:11.620 --> 00:03:16.120
The last we saw Lydia, she was looking significantly
under the weather when she called Todd, thinking

00:03:16.120 --> 00:03:18.920
that her plan to kill Walt had been successfully
carried out.

00:03:19.150 --> 00:03:23.080
Soon after, Walt tells her that not only had
her plan failed, but that her illness was

00:03:23.080 --> 00:03:25.430
in fact the first stages of ricin poisoning.

00:03:25.680 --> 00:03:29.420
While Breaking Bad implied that Lydia was
doomed, El Camino reveals that her fate may

00:03:29.420 --> 00:03:30.720
still be up in the air.

00:03:31.030 --> 00:03:34.980
At one point, Jesse hears a radio news report
that mentions a "Houston woman" with possible

00:03:34.980 --> 00:03:39.440
ties to Walter White is in the hospital in
critical condition and not expected to survive.

00:03:39.860 --> 00:03:43.920
However, while her odds don't look great,
we'll never know for sure if Walt was successful

00:03:43.920 --> 00:03:45.200
in his attempt to get rid of her.

00:03:45.360 --> 00:03:50.240
“Well, bye Lydia.”

00:03:52.220 --> 00:03:56.400
One of the most heartwarming parts of El Camino
comes right at the beginning, when a traumatized

00:03:56.409 --> 00:04:00.819
Jesse turns to two of the only allies he has
left his longtime friends Skinny Pete and

00:04:00.820 --> 00:04:01.320
Badger.

00:04:01.560 --> 00:04:05.240
However, after Pete and Badger help Jesse,
they hit a snag when they attempt to get rid

00:04:05.250 --> 00:04:09.530
of the El Camino that Jesse was driving: the
LoJack was activated, meaning the police will

00:04:09.530 --> 00:04:10.900
arrive at Pete's house soon.

00:04:11.080 --> 00:04:15.520
Jesse offers to drive the El Camino away from
the house, but Skinny Pete has another plan:

00:04:15.520 --> 00:04:19.579
Badger will abandon Pete's car near the Mexican
border, Jesse will escape in Badger's car,

00:04:19.580 --> 00:04:21.800
and Pete will remain at his house with the
El Camino.

00:04:22.120 --> 00:04:24.800
Pete and Badger also give Jesse all the money
they have on them.

00:04:24.960 --> 00:04:28.860
After Jesse and Badger drive off, Pete moves
the El Camino to the front of his driveway

00:04:28.860 --> 00:04:31.900
and waits for the police to arrive, showing
that he has nothing to hide.

00:04:32.160 --> 00:04:36.110
While the teaser for El Camino seemed to pick
up after this with Pete in the police station,

00:04:36.110 --> 00:04:39.199
the film itself never shows either of Jesse's
friends again.

00:04:39.199 --> 00:04:42.510
We can only hope that Pete and Badger get
to go home and keep working on their Star

00:04:42.510 --> 00:04:43.500
Trek spec script.

00:04:43.560 --> 00:04:45.380
"I ever tell you about my Star Trek script?"

00:04:46.640 --> 00:04:47.520
"Star Trek?"

00:04:47.580 --> 00:04:50.080
"Yeah, I gotta write it down is all.

00:04:50.400 --> 00:04:51.400
The enterprise…"

00:04:52.560 --> 00:04:56.420
In the penultimate scene of El Camino, as
Jesse prepares to embark on his new life in

00:04:56.430 --> 00:05:00.800
Alaska, Ed the Disappearer asks him if there's
anything else Jesse needs to take care of

00:05:00.800 --> 00:05:02.120
before the two part ways.

00:05:02.280 --> 00:05:06.420
Jesse hands him a letter which Ed reads over
and then promises to mail from Mexico City

00:05:06.420 --> 00:05:06.920
in a month.

00:05:07.140 --> 00:05:11.420
As Jesse drives away, the camera reveals that
the letter is addressed to Brock Cantillo.

00:05:11.480 --> 00:05:14.780
Neither of them discusses what Jesse wrote
in his final missive to Brock, although we

00:05:14.780 --> 00:05:17.460
can guess that at least part of his note was
a farewell.

00:05:17.720 --> 00:05:19.840
The rest is left up to our imaginations.

00:05:20.000 --> 00:05:24.090
Perhaps Jesse tried to offer some sort of
explanation or apology for what happened to

00:05:24.090 --> 00:05:24.580
his mother.

00:05:24.740 --> 00:05:28.000
It's also possible that Jesse used some of
the money he took from Neil Kandy to help

00:05:28.000 --> 00:05:31.940
provide for Brock's future, similar to the
trust Walt managed to set up for his son.

00:05:32.320 --> 00:05:36.120
We may never know what Jesse's final words
to Brock were, but no matter what he wrote,

00:05:36.120 --> 00:05:37.340
we're sure it came from the heart.

00:05:38.180 --> 00:05:42.000
The last we saw of Saul Goodman's intimidating
bodyguard Huell Babineaux toward the end of

00:05:42.000 --> 00:05:46.550
Breaking Bad, he was sitting in a DEA safehouse,
patiently awaiting the return of Hank Schrader

00:05:46.550 --> 00:05:47.700
and Steve Gomez.

00:05:47.870 --> 00:05:52.020
Unfortunately for everyone, Hank and Steve
were killed by Jack Welker and his gang shortly

00:05:52.040 --> 00:05:55.940
thereafter, so they wouldn't ever return to
the safehouse to advise Huell on next steps.

00:05:56.130 --> 00:06:00.260
According to series creator Vince Gilligan,
Huell would have eventually been found, questioned,

00:06:00.260 --> 00:06:02.740
and ultimately released by other DEA agents.

00:06:02.800 --> 00:06:06.280
But that's not really good enough for fans
who hoped to see Huell's fate definitively

00:06:06.290 --> 00:06:07.370
addressed in canon.

00:06:07.370 --> 00:06:11.520
The official Breaking Bad Facebook page took
it one step further, sharing a video of Huell

00:06:11.520 --> 00:06:15.140
getting up and leaving the safe house to coincide
with the release of El Camino.

00:06:15.260 --> 00:06:18.740
Still, Huell failed to get a cameo, or even
a mention, in the movie itself.

00:06:19.260 --> 00:06:23.130
Even if we consider the Facebook video part
of the film, all it establishes is that Huell

00:06:23.130 --> 00:06:24.949
eventually left the safe house.

00:06:24.949 --> 00:06:29.090
We have no idea where he went or what he's
up to now, and El Camino doesn't give us any

00:06:29.090 --> 00:06:29.780
clues.

00:06:30.460 --> 00:06:34.720
The other long-suffering employee in the office
of Saul Goodman &amp; Associates is Francesca

00:06:34.720 --> 00:06:39.280
Liddy, who we last saw toward the end of Breaking
Bad's final season, when she was held at gunpoint

00:06:39.280 --> 00:06:40.240
by Jesse Pinkman.

00:06:40.680 --> 00:06:44.880
Although Huell was later picked up by the
DEA, we never learn what became of Francesca

00:06:44.880 --> 00:06:48.440
after Saul fled Albuquerque and Saul Goodman
&amp; Associates was no more.

00:06:49.140 --> 00:06:52.880
In the Breaking Bad spinoff series Better
Call Saul, we learn that Francesca was once

00:06:52.889 --> 00:06:57.280
a bright-eyed and enthusiastic former employee
of New Mexico's Motor Vehicle Division.

00:06:57.280 --> 00:07:00.900
Somehow, over her years of working with Saul,
she became jaded and cynical.

00:07:01.130 --> 00:07:05.460
We wondered whether we might see her pop up
in El Camino, but the former receptionist/accomplice

00:07:05.460 --> 00:07:07.700
didn't receive a mention in the Jesse-centric
tale.

00:07:07.990 --> 00:07:11.560
We're not sure what professional opportunities
are out there for a secretary who spent the

00:07:11.560 --> 00:07:15.419
last decade of her life working for a shady
criminal lawyer who's currently wanted by

00:07:15.420 --> 00:07:16.300
the DEA.

00:07:16.420 --> 00:07:20.639
Still, Better Call Saul did leave us with
a few clues for where Francesca goes after

00:07:20.640 --> 00:07:21.880
the events of Breaking Bad.

00:07:22.130 --> 00:07:26.060
In the spinoff, we see that Saul gives Francesca
the business card of a lawyer from his Jimmy

00:07:26.060 --> 00:07:31.320
McGill days we may find out what happened
to Francesca in an upcoming season of BCS.

00:07:32.020 --> 00:07:36.410
For viewers of Better Call Saul, we've gotten
a small glimpse into what Saul Goodman, formerly

00:07:36.410 --> 00:07:39.700
known as Jimmy McGill, is up to following
the events of Breaking Bad.

00:07:39.950 --> 00:07:44.380
The last we saw him in Breaking Bad, Saul
was preparing to embark on a new life in Nebraska,

00:07:44.380 --> 00:07:46.020
courtesy of Ed the Disappearer.

00:07:46.330 --> 00:07:50.200
In Better Call Saul, we see that in his new
life, Saul is known as Gene, and he works

00:07:50.200 --> 00:07:51.520
at a Cinnabon in Omaha.

00:07:51.720 --> 00:07:55.100
Still afraid of the enemies he made through
his association with Walt, Gene lives in a

00:07:55.100 --> 00:07:57.379
constant state of anxiety and paranoia.

00:07:57.379 --> 00:08:01.110
While we may eventually get a more complete
picture of what Saul's life looks like following

00:08:01.110 --> 00:08:03.980
Breaking Bad, El Camino didn't offer up any
clues.

00:08:04.240 --> 00:08:08.080
The only obscure nod to Saul Goodman is a
brief shot of the strip mall that once housed

00:08:08.080 --> 00:08:10.940
his law office, which has since been turned
into a sports bar.

00:08:11.080 --> 00:08:15.160
Neither Jesse nor Ed ever discusses what became
of the disgraced former lawyer, and although

00:08:15.170 --> 00:08:19.330
Better Call Saul fills in the blanks a little
bit, there's still plenty we don't know about

00:08:19.330 --> 00:08:20.820
Saul's life following Breaking Bad.

00:08:21.060 --> 00:08:24.900
But if there's one thing we know about Saul
Goodman, it's that as much as he may insist

00:08:24.900 --> 00:08:29.030
he's left his former life behind him, he won't
be able to keep his nose clean for long.

00:08:30.170 --> 00:08:33.970
Throughout Breaking Bad, although it was never
stated outright, it was always implied that

00:08:33.970 --> 00:08:36.740
Jesse Pinkman dropped out of high school before
graduating.

00:08:37.100 --> 00:08:41.010
We knew that he failed Mr. White's chemistry
class as a junior, yet Jesse's parents still

00:08:41.010 --> 00:08:45.890
considered Walt one of Jesse's better teachers,
implying that his F in chemistry was not an

00:08:45.890 --> 00:08:47.320
anomaly on his report card.

00:08:47.690 --> 00:08:52.040
However, in El Camino, Walt comments that
Jesse might try college, suggesting a business

00:08:52.040 --> 00:08:55.580
and marketing degree as a counter to Jesse's
proposal of sports medicine.

00:08:55.740 --> 00:08:59.800
But first, Walt says, Jesse would have to
get his GED, to which Jesse responds that

00:08:59.800 --> 00:09:02.700
he doesn't need a GED because he already has
a high school diploma.

00:09:02.700 --> 00:09:06.020
"Yo, you were standing right on stage when
they handed it to me."

00:09:06.020 --> 00:09:07.380
"It just slipped my mind."

00:09:07.600 --> 00:09:10.100
"I totally graduated high school, dick."

00:09:10.800 --> 00:09:15.320
Of course, now that Jesse has a new identity
in Alaska as "Mr. Driscoll," he likely wouldn't

00:09:15.330 --> 00:09:19.410
be using his degree from J.P. Wynne High School
on his application, but that doesn't mean

00:09:19.410 --> 00:09:21.830
he can't continue his education under his
new name.

00:09:21.830 --> 00:09:26.150
If Jesse Pinkman has a completed high school
education, then so does Mr. Driscoll, and

00:09:26.150 --> 00:09:29.800
although few of Walter White's ideas ever
seemed to be in Jesse's best interest, this

00:09:29.800 --> 00:09:30.420
one might be.

00:09:30.720 --> 00:09:34.420
El Camino doesn't tell us what happens to
Jesse once he arrives in Alaska, but it's

00:09:34.420 --> 00:09:37.930
nice to think that if we were to catch up
with him at some point in the distant future,

00:09:37.930 --> 00:09:40.590
we'd find him with a successful career in
sports medicine.

00:09:40.590 --> 00:09:42.700
If not that, maybe he can major in...

00:09:42.940 --> 00:09:43.940
"Magnets!

00:09:44.000 --> 00:09:44.700
Oh!"

